        "original_id": "a45f071f-2e00-5b86-8bd4-38997897250b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Bank of British North America\n- Places: London, England; Toronto; Montreal; Quebec City; Saint John, New Brunswick; Halifax; St. John's, Newfoundland; Bay of Fundy; New Brunswick\n- Concepts: Royal Charter; population ranking\n\nFacts:\n- The Bank of British North America was founded in 1836 by a Royal Charter issued in London, England.\n- The Bank of British North America had offices in Toronto, Montreal, Quebec City, Saint John, New Brunswick, Halifax, and St. John's, Newfoundland.\n- Saint John is a port city on the Bay of Fundy in the Canadian province of New Brunswick.\n- In 2016, Saint John became the second most populous city in New Brunswick for the first time after decades of decline.\n- In 2016, Saint John had a population of 67,575 and an area of 315.82 square kilometres.",
